==Finnish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈluode(ʔ)/|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|luo|de|lang=fi}}

===Etymology 1===
Uncertain, possibly related to etymology 2. Cognate to Estonian {{m|et|loe||north-west}} and Karelian {{m|krl|luuveh||west, south-west}}.

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[northwest]]

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-hame|n=sg|luo|d|t|a}}

=====Related terms=====
{{compass-fi}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|fi|kaakko}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|fi|luoteinen}} = northwestern
* {{l|fi|luoteis-}} = northwest as adjective, like in luoteisväylä = northwest passage
* {{l|fi|luoteenpuoleinen}} = roughly northwestern, as of wind

===Etymology 2===
Originally meant flood or high tide; from a {{etyl|gem|fi}} language, a cognate of German {{m|de|Flut}}, Swedish {{m|sv|flod}}.

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[ebb]] (low tide)

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-hame|luo|d|t|a}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|fi|laskuvesi}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|fi|vuoksi}}

